# Shell Environment: Windows 11 + PowerShell 7

This machine runs **Windows 11** with **PowerShell 7.x** as the shell. All terminal commands execute as `.ps1` scripts.

## Rules

- NEVER use bash-only syntax: `cat <<'EOF'`, heredocs, `$(...)` subshells, `&&` chaining in complex cases
- Use `-m "single line message"` for git commits instead of heredocs
- For multi-line strings use PowerShell here-strings (`@'...'@`) if absolutely needed
- NEVER use `cat`, `head`, `tail`, `sed`, `awk`, `grep` — use the dedicated Read, Write, StrReplace, Grep tools instead
- `&&` works for simple command chaining in pwsh 7, but avoid mixing with bash-isms
- File paths use backslashes (`C:\...`) but forward slashes also work in most contexts
- Environment variables: `$env:VAR_NAME` (not `$VAR_NAME`)

